        "PMC8510135::rubric_card::000::d6d90d1989"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Conventional processing typically requires temperatures above 1700 °C to attain similar densification.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical alloying produces high-surface-area powder.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mechanical alloying increases lattice-defect density and grain-boundary area.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The lattice defects introduced by mechanical alloying lower the activation energy for diffusion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The pulsed electric current and rapid heating associated with SPS facilitate densification.",
